      "hints": [
        "Separate variables as $dx/[(20-x)(40-x)]=dt/5$.",
        "Decompose the left side into $A/(20-x)+B/(40-x)$ and determine $A,B$.",
        "Integrate logarithmically and apply $x=10$ at $t=0$.",
        "Combine the logarithms, exponentiate to obtain a rational relation involving $e^{4t}$, and solve algebraically for $x$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Separate variables and integrate one side",
        "Obtain the term $0.2t$",
        "Use partial fractions, e.g. $1/((20-x)(40-x))=A/(20-x)+B/(40-x)$",
        "Obtain $A=1/20$ and $B=-1/20$",
        "Integrate to obtain $-(1/20)\\ln(20-x)+(1/20)\\ln(40-x)$, or equivalent",
        "Use $x=10$, $t=0$ to evaluate the constant, or use limits",
        "Obtain a correct intermediate solution in any form",
        "Obtain $x=(60e^{4t}-40)/(3e^{4t}-1)$, or equivalent",
        "$x=\\frac{60e^{4t}-40}{3e^{4t}-1}$."
      ],
